# ─── Vivado generated / temporary files ──────────────────────────────────────

# Project cache (fully regenerable)
*.cache/
.Xil/

# Vivado run outputs (synthesis, implementation, simulation results)
*.runs/
*.sim/

# Vivado journal and log files
vivado.jou
vivado.log
vivado_*.backup.jou
vivado_*.backup.log

# Vivado HLS
*.ap_proj/
solution*/
*.zip

# Bitstream and hardware handoff
*.bit
*.bin
*.ltx
*.xsa
*.hdf

# Webtalk / usage statistics
.Xil/
webtalk*.log
webtalk*.jou
usage_statistics_webtalk*.html
usage_statistics_webtalk*.xml

# Hardware manager
*.hw/

# ─── IP generated output products ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The .gen/ directory contains large auto-generated IP output products.
# Vivado can re-generate these from the .xci files in .srcs/.
# Uncomment the line below to exclude them (reduces repo size significantly).
# *.gen/

# ─── OS / editor artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ─── v2 per-stage build trees ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each stage's build.tcl creates a self-contained stageN/ Vivado project
# under v2/boards/zed_fmcs3/. Fully regenerable -- don't track.
v2/boards/zed_fmcs3/stage*/
v2/ip/synth_check_proj/

# ─── Cloned dependencies (not tracked here, see README) ──────────────────────
adi-hdl/
adi-no-os/
openwifi-hw/

# ─── Old simulation/exploration project (lives on `main`, not here) ──────────
# This branch is v2-only. The simulation TB, IP_user_files and IP gen
# trees from the prior project are NOT carried on this branch.
ofdmTxRx.cache/
ofdmTxRx.gen/
ofdmTxRx.hw/
ofdmTxRx.ip_user_files/
ofdmTxRx.runs/
ofdmTxRx.sim/
ofdmTxRx.srcs/
ofdmTxRx.xpr
openofdm_transceiver_tb_behav.wcfg

# ─── Per-user / per-machine working artefacts ────────────────────────────────
# Local Vitis workspaces, scratch CSVs, build outputs from ad-hoc scripts.
build/
sw/
Users/
*.csv

# ─── Keep these ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source Verilog/VHDL, IP configs (.xci), coefficient files (.coe),
# memory init files (.mem), project file (.xpr), and waveform configs (.wcfg)
# under v2/ are all tracked — do NOT add them above.
